Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||08-03-2000||07:13 PM||||<BR>I just got done work on my 84 SE but i'm know where near happy with it, I have fixed the random reving of the engine at idle with a "GOOD" IAC valve from my parts car. Now the car starts right up and idles @ 2000 RPM when the car warms up it seems to be fine but if I turn it off and try to start it again It won't start at all. I started playing W/ the timing and it will fire a few times but not start. Please help me I just dumped alot of money into this crappy 2.5<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-03-2000||09:21 PM||||need more info....... no spark? no fuel? anything else?<P>did you take off the tach filter yet? those will kill the spark if they are bad. The filter can develope thermal problems. The car will run w/o it. the tach just won't work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||08-03-2000||10:17 PM||||There is Fule after a few second of cranking (30sec or more) I can smell it from my exhaust pipe, There is some spark I don't know if it's enough though how can I check if I have enough spark. I does run but I can't start it back up after It gets hot I have oil I do not have a Thermostat during the summer (I have a new PROM burned for this for this). <P>  Is the Tach filter is the sensor in the block to the right of the distributor? I unpluged what i thought was the tach filter, The tach still worked the car did not.<P> I just instaled a Weapon R carbon Intake, DC sports free flow exhaust, Holley 300 TBI, Custom Ram air and a  custom Computer from a 86(2.5) SE with chip set. can theies "messup" my car?||||reg||9
Z||000003||Dan87GT||08-04-2000||09:03 AM||||I know in my 86SE V6, I had hot starting problems. After rebuilding the distributor, swapping the fuel rail and injectors, and replacing the coolant temp sensor. I finally noticed I could smell fuel and figured it was flooding out. Replaced the cold start valve and sensor, problem solved. A good check would to be to floor the accelerator to put the ECM in flood mode, if it starts its probably a faulty cold start injector or sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Xtreme Fiero's||08-04-2000||10:36 AM||||I just checked the ECM codes twice one hot and once cold, the first time (cold) I got the folowing 12,34,12 the second time (hot) i got 12,15,34,12. Hot i got Coolant and map sensor codes. Is the coolant sensor stoping my car from starting? It cant be the MAP can it? Iv'e driven with out my MAP beforew/ no problem the computer just compensates by using the TPS to control the fuel my car usualy rus better without the map pluged in<P>P.S. my temp never gets above 150-160.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||08-04-2000||10:57 AM||||The 2.5 doesn't have a cold start valve. The temp sensor will not prevent starting. Try this, start the car and let it warm up, turn off, attempt restart (won't work?) disconnect the MAP sensor plug only and attempt to start (you cantry to substitute a good sensor at this time as well) and see what it does.<BR>Get back with me.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Xtreme Fiero's||08-04-2000||04:15 PM||||     <BR>    Where is the tach filter? My car has been setup to run with out the MAP sensor I have about 1000 miles on the car with the new 86 computer and chip. The chip was custom burned for a turbo knock sensor, High flow exhaust/intake, No MAP, no Thermostat and to run on 110 octane fuel. The new computer also has a second/sister unit for Boost control, Timing control and two (hot/cold) PC programable "MAP" map's. I belive my "Hot" MAP is not properly set but on a stock engine would the MAP stop the car from running?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||08-04-2000||08:29 PM||||In answer to the last '?'. The system is designed to run in an open loop in case the MAP sensor fails. It won't run correctly, but will get to where you need to be for service. In some cases however it won't run at all.<P>This situation is 'stock' set-up.<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 08-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||08-05-2000||08:12 PM||||All those changes...... could be anything. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Xtreme Fiero's||08-05-2000||08:24 PM||||I just set two new Timing and MAP sensor "MAP's" the car now idles @ 800-1100 RPM. IT wont rev past 3000 rpm now but that is a timing problem Thanks to every one who helped me out.||||reg||10
Z||000010||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2000||10:21 PM||||Just checking up to see! That was my next suggestion, was the 'low side' MAP missing proper values?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Xtreme Fiero's||08-07-2000||09:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>Just checking up to see! That was my next suggestion, was the 'low side' MAP missing proper values?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>OK the way my computer system in my car is setup so that my Factory 86 SE computer controls everything but the sensors that control/send voltage, My secondary computer is PC programable to control Low MAP (0°-150°), High MAP (150°-250°), advance TPS (dumps more fuel) Varible Timing Eletronic Control system (VTEC) It also controls the fan switch and coolant sensor for orignal ECM.<P>   All the stster system does is plug into the TPS, MAP, O2, Knock coolant sensors and the distributor Then you set values for them to get the max for your engine. in short it is a factory setup but the ECM is not conected to the engine.<P>   My problem was that @ 150° the system switches to a "HOT MAP" this had never been saved properly so all I Did there was duplicate the "Cold MAP" and give a tittle more voltage. the timing system is wat stoped my car from starting, my car has a HKS knock sensor for use up to 30 PSI of boost with it hooked up to my computer it is set to give a big ass 25° retard if the engine knocks, well my timing was set 7°BTDC the engine was hot and the factory ecm would advance the timing on a start and knock once the BAM I had 32° BTDC, I set timing @ 10° BTDC and blocked off the Vac. advance in the distributor. and it runs now. the timing still ned to be setup buy a pro. next week i've got an apointmet @ the local HONDA dealer so they can set the timing/VTEC system.<BR>||||reg||1
